# A handbrake turn in the crew van (game/vehicles.ts, docs/mechanics/driving.md), on the wide road by the
# park gate. Up to about 12 m/s heading east, then the handbrake (slide) with full right: the rear lets go
# (grip.handbrake), the spin builds (grip.yawBoost, yawAccel) and dies away only slowly (yawFade), so in
# 1.2 s the van swaps ends while it slides on east; then up (the brake against the slide, then the
# throttle): it stops and drives off west. The same approach with the steering alone (after a fresh
# summon) turns the way the tyres' grip allows: some 40 degrees in the same time, carving wide.
park sf
cmd 0 traffic clear
cmd 1 van summon 10 -5 90
cmd 2 teleport 10 -2.6 -0.2 90
tap use 30
hold up 40..340
hold slide 340..482
hold right 340..482
hold up 490..700
cmd 899 vehicle exit
cmd 900 van summon 10 -5 90
cmd 901 teleport 10 -2.6 -0.2 90
tap use 930
hold up 940..1240
hold right 1240..1360
run 1400
expect event vehicleEnter{name=crew_van} count == 2
expect no event vanBump
expect van.hspeed > 11.5 at 340
expect van.heading > 180 at 440
expect van.heading > 240 at 490
expect van.vel.x > 5 at 480
expect van.hspeed < 1 at 570
expect van.vel.x < -5 at 700
expect van.heading < 135 at 1360
expect van.hspeed > 11 at 1360
